Quoting  pdpi <pdpinheiro@gmail.com>:
>Why is it that people advise you to use the pickaxe (1d6 damage, 3.5
>avg/1 min) instead of the +2 whip (3.5 avg/3 min), except where it
>pertains to thick-skinned monsters?

Bear in mind that lower minimum damage goes with higher maximum damage.
Admittedly the pick-axe wastes some of that maximum on overkill.

Actually, notwithstanding the mattock (explained elsewhere), I would stick
with the whip for as long as you are missing monsters.

>How is it that people tend to get their hands on silver sabres? I never
>seem to find any.

This simply isn't a consideration early on. There aren't any silver-hating
monsters except werecreatures and there's little point pre-practicing the
skill for Grayswandir when once you have Grayswandir you can easily
practice the skill.

>Besides these specific issues, is there any sort of global strategy to
>follow regaring archeologists?

Not much beyond that for any other fragile character. Bear in mind you are
Fast, making retreats easier (and also making it easier to fight on
terrain of your choosing); and digging out a few vaults or finding a few
gems can easily allow you to get all the goodies in every shop you find.
